WEBVTT

00:01:29.412 --> 00:01:36.168
including the blue gift bag
that's dressed up as the flag of Scotland.

00:01:36.192 --> 00:01:38.477
I put this picture online,
and sure enough,

00:01:38.501 --> 00:01:41.466
within the first few minutes,
someone left a comment that said,

00:01:41.490 --> 00:01:44.945
"You can take that Scottish Saltire
and shove it up your ass."

00:01:44.969 --> 00:01:46.697
(Laughter)

00:01:46.721 --> 00:01:49.019
See, people are passionate
about flags, you know?

00:01:49.043 --> 00:01:50.337
That's the way it is.

00:01:50.361 --> 00:01:51.900
What I love about flags

00:01:51.924 --> 00:01:54.195
is that once you understand
the design of flags,

00:01:54.219 --> 00:01:56.789
what makes a good flag,
what makes a bad flag,

00:01:56.813 --> 00:01:59.372
you can understand
the design of almost anything.

00:01:59.396 --> 00:02:01.183
So what I'm going to do here is,